# name: test/sql/replacement_scan_registration.test
# description: The replacement scan is registered on EVERY load path, so bare FROM works
# group: [sql]

require markdown

# =============================================================================
# `FROM '<path>'` with no reader function goes through the replacement scan,
# which is registered in LoadInternal. It used to be registered in
# MarkdownExtension::Load instead -- a function the LOADABLE extension's entry
# point (markdown_duckdb_cpp_init, via DUCKDB_CPP_EXTENSION_ENTRY) never calls.
#
# So the loadable build registered every table function and no replacement scan:
# read_markdown('x.md') worked while FROM 'x.md' raised
#
#   Binder Error: No extension found that is capable of reading the file "x.md"
#
# This was NOT a DuckDB 2.0 regression, though #82 assumed one. The entry macro
# expands identically on v1.5.6 and v2.0-cyanoptera and the failure reproduces on
# a stock v1.5.6 CLI; static builds hid it because they run Load().
#
# WHAT THIS FILE CAN AND CANNOT SEE. Run by `unittest`, these assertions exercise
# whichever load path that binary uses -- statically linked, they would pass even
# with the defect restored. They are still worth pinning: they fail loudly on a
# loadable run, which is what the community-extensions next-line leg does, and
# they document the contract. The discriminating check is to LOAD the built
# .duckdb_extension into a STOCK duckdb of the same version, where pre-fix both
# queries below raise the binder error and post-fix both return 1.
# =============================================================================

# Plain path, no decoration, no glob.
query I
SELECT count(*) FROM 'test/markdown/simple.md';
----
1

# A glob still routes through the same scan.
query I
SELECT count(*) > 0 FROM 'test/markdown/*.md';
----
true

# An explicit reader call does NOT depend on the replacement scan, so it keeps
# working even when the scan is missing. It is the control that proves the two
# assertions above are testing the scan and not merely "the extension loaded".
query I
SELECT count(*) FROM read_markdown('test/markdown/simple.md');
----
1
